---
source: crates/agent-compose/tests/cli.rs
expression: stdout(&output)
---
Run one flow, declared manual trigger or not (validates, builds, then launches; `--no-build` launches the built tree as it stands)

Usage: agent-compose run [OPTIONS] <PATH> <FLOW>

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          Path to the spec entrypoint (conventionally `main.yml`)

  <FLOW>
          The flow to run, as a typed address (`flow.<name>`)

Options:
      --input <FIELD=VALUE>
          One input binding, repeatable: `--input goal=ship it`

      --session <KEY>
          The session identity session-scoped stores key off (grammar 11.3)

      --target <NAME>
          Deploy target to resolve and emit for
          
          [default: local]

      --out <DIR>
          Where to write the generated project [default: <project>/build/<target>]

      --no-build
          Launch the project already built in the output directory as it stands: no validation, no build, and the spec is not read

      --format <FORMAT>
          How to report what was found, and how the run answers

          Possible values:
          - human: Written for a person, on stderr
          - json:  One JSON object on stdout
          
          [default: human]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
